cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Spikeling, please cite it as below."
title: "Spikeling: a DSL and multi-backend runtime for spiking neural networks"
abstract: >-
  A compact domain-specific language (.spk) for describing spiking neural
  networks, with one description running unchanged on four backends: an
  interactive Python runtime with STDP, generated C for embedded targets,
  generated Verilog for FPGA simulation, and GDScript for driving game AI.
  Includes LIF / Izhikevich / AdEx / Resonator neuron types, a hardware
  sensor-adapter layer, and an MCP tool surface.
type: software
